Hi,

Four fixes for the ibmveth driver. They apply to net-next as is and
do not depend on the two open() error-path fixes recently applied to
net (af0524bf4ce1, 84bec0bf0352); patch 2 explains how it relates to
them. Three of the bugs can take the networking stack down with no
recovery short of a reboot; the fourth is memory corruption.

They target net-next rather than net: the triggers are rare (an
open() failure during a direct reopen, PHYP returning a bad
correlator, netconsole under TX contention) and there are no field
reports. All four carry Fixes: tags and are suitable for stable once
merged; I can repost them against net if you prefer.

Patch 1 removes ndo_poll_controller. It ran replenish from netpoll
outside NAPI with no lock, racing NAPI's replenish on the same pool:
a free slot could be posted to PHYP twice. The callback is
unnecessary since netpoll polls NAPI itself, as was done for
ibmvnic.

Patch 2 stops a second close() after a failed direct reopen.
change_mtu, the pool sysfs store, set_csum and set_tso close and
reopen the device directly; if that open() fails, IFF_UP stays set
and the next ndo_stop napi_disable()s an already-disabled NAPI with
RTNL held. The hang is deterministic once open() has failed, and it
also blocks shutdown.

Patch 3 rejects correlators that name an inactive buffer pool, which
passed the size check and dereferenced a NULL skbuff array in
softirq.

Patch 4 makes poll step past a bad RX slot. Since 2c91e2319ed9
turned the correlator BUG_ON()s into WARN_ON() plus a reset, poll
breaks out without advancing the ring and restarts on the same slot
forever, and the reset meant to recover deadlocks in napi_disable()
against that loop. The WARN_ON()s on PHYP-supplied data become a
ratelimited error.

Each commit message says how the bug was found and how the fix was
tested. In short: ibmveth KUnit suite on qemu pseries (ppc64le)
passes, and the new cases in patches 3 and 4 fail on the unfixed
driver; @@HW-COVER: LPAR model/firmware and what was run@@.

